From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:30:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/43] Probe end criterion: stop once every probe has settled
 (OPENEMS_PROBE_END_DB)

The energy end criterion never fires on real boards: the pulse's static charge
keeps the total energy at -11 to -13 dB for ever, so runs go to max_time while
the port signals have decayed below -80 dB a quarter of the way in.

With OPENEMS_PROBE_END_DB=-60 (and OPENEMS_PROBE_END_HOLD, default 1 excitation
length) RunFDTD stops once every enabled integral probe (port voltages and
currents, field probes) has stayed below that fraction of its own peak for the
hold time, i.e. the port-signal settle test post-processing applies anyway, done
inside the run. Gaussian excitation only; a probe whose peak is below 1e-6 of
the largest of its kind is measured against that peak; off unless the variable
is set, so fixed-NrTS runs are untouched (bit-identical to the previous build).
ProcessIntegral keeps the peak and the latest |integral| of each probe.
verbose>1 lists the probes, verbose>2 traces every check.

Full rfsim runs, engine auto threads: GCPW line 94217 -> 45570 timesteps
(17.7 -> 8.9 s), SMA launch 188697 -> 107289 (182 -> 99 s); the early-stopped
port files are a bit-identical prefix of the full run's, S21 within 1e-3 dB.

